or mechanism-breaking than conservation-matched controls.', '6. Layer and scale analysis: Report where mechanism-selectivity emerges across layers and how it changes from ESM-2 150M to 650M to 3B (as compute allows), testing whether larger models are more mechanistic or more correlational.', '7. Baselines: Compare against categorical-Jacobian coevolution features and PSSM-based baselines to show that any observed mechanism-selectivity is not explained by coevolutionary statistics alone.'], 'Risk Factors and Limitations': ['Confound: buried-charged mutations also disrupt evolutionary statistics, so mechanism-preserving controls must be carefully matched on conservation change; if matching is imperfect, causal attribution weakens. We mitigate with explicit conservation-matched control mutations.', 'Features may be distributed/superposed such that no single feature cleanly maps to one mechanism; we address this using both SAE features and probe directions and reporting aggregate directions.', 'Molecular-mechanics ddG estimates (FoldX) are approximate and may be noisy, limiting the strength of the physics-agreement comparison.', 'Results may reveal that models are largely correlational; while scientifically valuable, this could be seen as a negative result — we frame it as a definitive answer either way with implications for variant-effect trust.', 'Access to ESM-2 3B and structure datasets is feasible for an academic lab, but running SAEs on 3B activations is compute-heavy; we scope the main study to 150M/650M with 3B as an extension.']}

